<p>A 21-year-old Austrian identified under local privacy rules as Beran A. pleaded guilty as his trial opened in Wiener Neustadt, Austria, in a case over a plot to attack a Taylor Swift concert in Vienna in August 2024. Prosecutors accuse him of pledging allegiance to Islamic State, spreading its propaganda online and preparing an attack tied to one of Swift’s Eras Tour shows at Ernst Happel Stadium. The plot led Austrian authorities to cancel all three of Swift’s scheduled Vienna performances, where more than 195,000 people were expected across the concerts. Authorities arrested Beran A. on Aug. 7, 2024, the day before the first concert, after an intelligence tip; prosecutors said police later found bomb-making material or an almost completed bomb during a search. Beran A. is being tried alongside another 21-year-old man, Arda K., on terrorism-related charges; only Beran A. is charged in connection with the Swift concert plot. Prosecutors also accuse the men and a third person of involvement in planned attacks abroad during Ramadan 2024, including in Saudi Arabia, Turkey and the United Arab Emirates, though those attacks were not carried out.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OEnVs9fUuEfOtb3nvEWHyHsvqbyFl28qxeHZ_HhTAZrlMWSI4ZcEofhHCSI5RWDSKAwu38c1bPAHbXB-Trobec8fFG0bpvs4PW-MtyPqKCi76nMHqyEOOovs7cdcFrpj26RJ-gWzC1tRHp4s50aE3RtRuRGJMBQqb4P2asKvKQjLuqS4mADixVye5qJr9wfKC1MB8DLh0pPtxyCvQheSw2XwT7Ta7ktGDPb3Hh80HmvpbXFvhVXd3eaK36bgJzd3gerNrMkaJ0bTgg4g6g' alt='Defendant Beran A. is led out of the courtroom on the first day of his trial over a Taylor Swift concert plot in Wiener Neustadt, Austria.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Target area: Authorities said in 2024 that the suspect planned to target crowds outside Ernst Happel Stadium, where up to 30,000 people could gather while 65,000 were inside.</li><li>Possible sentence: The charges include terrorism offenses and membership in a terrorist organization, with a possible sentence of up to 20 years in prison.</li><li>Illegal purchases: Prosecutors said Beran A. tried to buy firearms and a hand grenade through illegal channels and received instructions on handling explosives from Islamic State-linked contacts.</li><li>Second defendant: Die Presse reported that Arda K. partially admitted accusations tied to a planned attack in Istanbul, while prosecutors accused the defendants of forming an Islamic State cell.</li></ul><blockquote>My client has caused a great deal of fear and panic among many people, and he will have to answer for that, no question. But please try to look beyond the headlines. - Anna Mair</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Austrian prosecutors: Prosecutors described the alleged Vienna plan as a suicide attack prepared for one of Swift’s concerts. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/04/28/concert-de-taylor-swift-vise-par-un-attentat-a-vienne-le-proces-du-principal-suspect-s-ouvre-en-autriche_6683904_3210.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Defense lawyer Anna Mair: Mair said outside court that Beran A. deeply regretted his actions and called them the biggest mistake of his life. (<a href='https://sentinelcolorado.com/a-town-magazine/celebrities/man-pleads-guilty-to-plotting-attack-on-a-taylor-swift-concert-in-vienna-austrian-media-report/'>Sentinel Colorado</a>)</li><li>Taylor Swift: Swift said after the cancellations that she was grateful to authorities because fans were &quot;grieving concerts and not lives,&quot; according to Arise News. (<a href='https://www.arise.tv/terror-trial-opens-over-alleged-plot-to-bomb-taylor-swift-vienna-concert/'>Arise News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/apr/28/austrian-man-goes-on-trial-for-2024-taylor-swift-concert-terror-plot'>Austrian man pleads guilty to plotting attack on Taylor Swift concert in Vienna</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/28/man-pleads-guilty-in-austria-to-plotting-attack